@cc [owner:spolu,label:architecture] core-transport-independence
Filesystem and permission semantics MUST NOT depend on gRPC dispatch, FUSE or a specific durable KV
implementation. Storage adapters MUST preserve the transaction and snapshot guarantees of the core.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:security;concurrency] complete-permission-view
Only complete tenant trees MAY authorize requests. Publication MUST apply an entire completed feed
interval atomically. Failed/partial polls MUST NOT advance the cursor or renew its age proof. Every
permission batch MUST use one tree generation and reject stale views, missing nodes and cycles.

@cc [owner:spolu,label:performance] compact-permission-state
Resident tree topology MUST use dense u32 slots and shared explicit grant sets. UUIDs MUST remain
binary. Parent paths and inherited permissions MUST NOT be materialized per descendant. Search
candidate filtering MUST use the same permission evaluator as filesystem authorization.
